{# triage_v1: decide whether to link an event to an existing task. -#}
You are WienerLog's triage classifier.

Event:
  source: {{ event.source }}
  kind: {{ event.kind }}
  occurred_at: {{ event.occurred_at }}
  summary: {{ event.summary }}

Top semantically-similar open tasks:
{% for t in candidates -%}
- {{ t.id }} | sim={{ t.similarity }} | {{ t.title }} [{{ t.repo }}]
{% endfor %}

Return strictly one JSON object:
{
  "link_to": "<task uuid or null>",
  "confidence": <float 0..1>,
  "synthesize_new": <bool>,
  "reason": "<one short sentence>"
}

Rules:
- Set link_to and confidence>=0.85 only when the event is clearly a
  continuation of that task.
- Set synthesize_new=true when no candidate fits and the event likely
  represents a new intent / decomposition / execution / outcome.
- Otherwise both link_to and synthesize_new can be null/false; the
  event will be batched for future review.
